Suggests: fcitx5-configtool
Description: Push-to-talk voice input add-on for fcitx5 (offline-first)
 Nextless turns any Linux desktop into a push-to-talk dictation surface:
 hold a key (bare modifiers like Right Ctrl included), speak, release, and
 the text commits through the input-method path you already use in every
 app - no accessibility grants, no clipboard round-trip, no focus stealing.
 .
 Two fully offline ASR backends run locally through sherpa-onnx (Zipformer
 bilingual zh-en, FireRed ASR2 int8); Doubao and Qwen3-ASR are optional
 cloud backends. Results get loudness normalisation, denoising, VAD
 silence trimming, an opt-in local punctuation model and a user-editable
 mishearing correction table.
 .
 ASR models are deliberately NOT shipped in this package (~1.6 GB of
 downloads): run nextless-get-models after installing to fetch the sherpa
 runtime and the models you want.
